    "created_at": "2025-05-08T00:03:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-08T00:03:36Z",
    "body": "In Chromium,\n- while showing a popover, [both the invoker and implicit anchor are set](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_element.cc;l=1591;drc=01c94ee4ea08a1d27bc877f5f78b533415c2ad02) after the `beforetoggle` event, and after handling auto/hint popover stacks and closings. This makes some sense to me, because e.g. if you cancel `beforetoggle` on this popover or others that get closed, you don't want to set either of these relationships up.\n- while hiding a popover, the [invoker is cleared](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_element.cc;l=1818;drc=01c94ee4ea08a1d27bc877f5f78b533415c2ad02) before the `beforetoggle` event but after hiding nested auto/hint popovers. That feels a bit early to me - since again you could cancel the `beforetoggle`. Perhaps this should move to after `beforetoggle`? I'd have to see what breaks if I try that.\n- while hiding a popover, the [implicit anchor is cleared](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc;l=8144;drc=2e87e014afa5464f87909bfa795ab10834459ed7) when the element is removed from the top layer (either immediately or after discrete `overlay` animations complete). That makes perfect sense to me, since you need it to stay related so that anchor positioning keeps working during exit transitions.\n\n\nIn the spec,\n- while [showing a popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#show-popover), steps 23 and 24 set both the invoker and implicit anchor after the `beforetoggle` event and after handling auto/hint popover stacks and closings. This matches Chromium.\n- while [hiding a popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hide-popover-algorithm), step 9 clears the invoker, before firing `beforetoggle` but after hiding nested auto/hint popovers. This matches Chromium, but as mentioned above, perhaps this should move to after `beforetoggle`, between steps 11 and 12?\n- while hiding a popover, step 10.5 clears the implicit anchor, but that's wrong. I think, for the reasons mentioned above, that it should be cleared in CSS's [remove an element from the top layer immediately](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#remove-an-element-from-the-top-layer-immediately). I have no idea how to connect that CSS spec algorithm with HTML's implicit anchor concept. I guess an HTML version of that algorithm gets created that can call the CSS version and then do the additional work?\n\nSo, in my reading, there's perhaps one change to make to both Chromium and the spec, and one pure-spec fix. Thoughts?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
