    "updated_at": "2025-05-10T00:02:48Z",
    "body": "> * while hiding a popover, the [invoker is cleared](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_element.cc;l=1818;drc=01c94ee4ea08a1d27bc877f5f78b533415c2ad02) before the `beforetoggle` event but after hiding nested auto/hint popovers. That feels a bit early to me - since again you could cancel the `beforetoggle`. Perhaps this should move to after `beforetoggle`? I'd have to see what breaks if I try that.\n\nI [tried this](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6520560), and tests don't seem to break. That makes me inclined to say this is likely web compatible. So I'm supportive of this change, if folks agree.",
