    "created_at": "2025-05-15T21:05:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-15T21:05:50Z",
    "body": "> while hiding a popover, step 10.5 clears the implicit anchor, but that's wrong. I think, for the reasons mentioned above, that it should be cleared in CSS's [remove an element from the top layer immediately](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#remove-an-element-from-the-top-layer-immediately). I have no idea how to connect that CSS spec algorithm with HTML's implicit anchor concept. I guess an HTML version of that algorithm gets created that can call the CSS version and then do the additional work?\n\nJust a nitpick for @tabatkins but \"process top layer removals\" should probably invoke the \"remove an element from the top layer immediately\" algorithm: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#process-top-layer-removals\n\nIt currently doesn't so you'd end up with a dangling implicit anchor without that change.",
