    "created_at": "2025-05-15T21:42:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-15T21:42:04Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure I fully understand the issue here, but if\n> \n> > I tried things like setting it back to `display:block` and changing its `id`, but I can't get anything observable in the focus order.\n> \n> is about how to make things focusable, usually setting `tabindex=\"0\"` on them does the trick.\n\nYeah, I tried that also. It's tricky to come up with a repro. You have to:\n 1. Show a popover that (I think) contains something focusable.\n 2. Set up a `beforetoggle` event handler that somehow observes that the invoker has been cleared, or sets some state that can be observed later.\n 3. Hide the popover. \n\nThe thing is that step 3 will hide the popover for sure, since `beforetoggle` isn't cancelable in this case. And showing the popover again will reset the invoker. So you either need to be able to see the focus navigation order somehow *during* step 2, or *do* something in step 2 that leaves the popover in a state that can be observed later, even while it is closed. Hence I tried setting `display:block` to see if I could observer (even manually) the focus order afterwards. I could not find anything that seems to work.\n\n> Also, is this testable even manually? That would give us some clues.\n> \n> If not, then I guess this is really just an editorial spec refactoring?\n\nI'm good with a manual test, but I couldn't find even that.\n",
